dialogue joined_holds
title: A word given
trigger: Joined holds
speaker commander $commander
speaker hero $hero

node open commander
  The newcomer from the Free Holds has polished their gear twice since supper and is starting a third time.
  * You took your time deciding. I'm glad you decided on us. -> walked
    if: TrustAtLeast $hero 15
  * You've joined the caravan. Before you march with us, talk with me. -> signed

node walked hero
  In the holds you don't give your word to strangers. I watched how you treat the ones who follow you. That was what decided it.
  -> oath

node signed hero
  I took the place that was offered. Where I come from, that isn't nothing. A hold remembers who opened the gate.
  -> oath

node oath hero
  I swore an oath to my hold once. Then the Captain sold our tithe to the Choir and called it peace. So I ask you plainly: what do you want sworn?
  -> swear

node swear commander
  The fire pops. Somewhere behind the wagons a horse stamps in its sleep.
  * Nothing. Stay because you choose to, every morning. -> choose
    do: AddTrust $hero 8
  * Swear to the people in the holds, not to me. -> people
    do: AddTrust $hero 6
  * Swear to follow my orders. That's all I need. -> orders
    do: AddTrust $hero -5

node choose hero
  No oath at all. My grandfather would call that dangerous. I think it might be the most honest offer anyone's made me.
  -> captain

node people hero
  The holds. The ones who paid and paid and got Hollow neighbours back for it. Yes. That I can swear to.
  -> captain

node orders hero
  The Captain wanted that too. I'll follow your orders, Commander, but I won't swear to them. Not again.
  -> captain

node captain hero
  You should know one thing. The Captain is still out there, hunting the runaways who took the Choir's caravan. Hunting you. Hunting me now.
  -> answer

node answer commander
  The hold-knight's hand rests on their sword hilt, without gripping it.
  * Then we face the Captain together, when the time comes. -> together
    do: AddTrust $hero 6
  * The Captain broke the holds' word. We'll make it right. -> right
    do: AddTrust $hero 8
  * Let the Captain hunt. We'll be gone before the dogs catch the scent. -> gone
    do: AddTrust $hero 2

node together hero
  Together. Good. I'd rather stand in that line beside someone than hear about it later from the road.

node right hero
  Make it right. You say it like you mean it. Then my shield goes where you go.

node gone hero
  Running isn't the holds' way. But I've seen what the Captain brings, so I'll run with you, for now.
